{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-10-11T06:23:15.913Z","author":"codex-agent","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"codex","agent_model":"gpt-6.1-sol","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"93dd497e28b8ee6af0f5a4db","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"gpt-6.1-sol","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"high","source":"probe"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":null},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-csv-0rvm"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"Make repeated terminal keyed CSV imports idempotent"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"Dependency certification exposed a separate package behavior: reimporting a CSV row keyed to an already closed item applies its update and then calls pm close again, which the host refuses as already terminal. The current closure-field fix validates create and open-to-terminal transitions but does not change this repeated-import path. Reproduce with a real tracker: import a closed row with a stable key, then import changed row content with the same key and closed status. Preserve verified lifecycle state and report the applied update honestly."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":2},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["csv","follow-up","terminal"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-10-11T06:23:15.913Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-10-11T06:23:15.913Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"codex-agent"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"Normal and atomic repeated terminal keyed imports preserve item identity and do not fail only because the item is already terminal; real-tracker regression fails when only the changed behavior is reverted; validate the declared minimum and current host without weakening lifecycle checks"}],"before